/// Item handlers: moving items into and out of the containers of blocks, seen from one side, like
/// a hopper does.
///
/// An `item-handler` is a view of the slots of the container at a position. Its slots are
/// numbered from 0 and are the slots reachable through the side the handler was made for: a
/// furnace seen from below has the output slot first and the fuel slot second, seen from above
/// only the input slot. The side decides which slots can be filled and emptied, with the rules
/// the hoppers use (a brewing stand takes potions only from below, a furnace gives out only
/// empty buckets from its fuel slot, a shulker box takes no shulker box). With no side the
/// handler sees every slot, and only the validity of an item for a slot is checked.
///
/// The containers that have a handler are the block entities that hold items: chests (a double
/// chest is one handler with the slots of both halves), trapped chests, barrels, shulker boxes,
/// furnaces, smokers, blast furnaces, hoppers, brewing stands, dispensers, droppers, and the
/// plugin inventories made with `register-plugin-inventory`.
///
/// A handler holds the container it was made for. It keeps working after the block is gone, on a
/// container nobody can reach any more, so ask for a new handler when the block may have changed.
/// Changes made through a handler are marked, so they are saved and comparators see them. The
/// experience a furnace collects is dropped as orbs above the furnace when its output slot is
/// emptied through a handler, like a hopper does. Using these functions needs the `containers`
/// permission.
interface item-handler {
    use common.{block-pos};
    use item-stack.{item-stack};
    use %world.{%world, block-direction};

    resource item-handler {
        /// The number of slots the side can reach.
        slot-count: func() -> u32;

        /// A copy of the stack in a slot, none if the slot is empty or does not exist.
        get-stack: func(slot: u32) -> option<item-stack>;

        /// The most items the slot takes, before the max stack size of the item. 0 if the slot
        /// does not exist.
        get-slot-limit: func(slot: u32) -> u8;

        /// Whether the stack may be put into the slot through this side, no matter what the slot
        /// holds or how full it is.
        is-item-valid: async func(slot: u32, stack: borrow<item-stack>) -> bool;

        /// Puts the stack into one slot, or when `slot` is none into the slots in order, first on
        /// the stacks it merges with and then into empty slots. Returns what did not fit, none if
        /// everything went in. With `simulate` nothing changes and the result is what would be
        /// returned. The given stack is not changed.
        insert: async func(slot: option<u32>, stack: borrow<item-stack>, simulate: bool) -> option<item-stack>;

        /// Takes up to `amount` items out of a slot, as far as this side may take them. Returns
        /// the items taken, none if there are none. With `simulate` nothing changes.
        extract: func(slot: u32, amount: u8, simulate: bool) -> option<item-stack>;
    }

    /// The item handler of the container at a position, seen from `side` (the face of the block
    /// the items go through). With no side the handler sees every slot. None if the chunk is not
    /// loaded or the block has no container, or the plugin lacks the `containers` permission.
    get-item-handler: func(target-world: borrow<%world>, pos: block-pos, side: option<block-direction>) -> option<item-handler>;

    /// Gives the plugin block entity at a position an inventory of `slot-count` slots (at most
    /// 4096) that take `slot-limit` items at most (1 to 99), or resizes the one it has. Growing
    /// keeps the items, shrinking fails if a slot that would go is not empty. The inventory is
    /// saved with the entity, every slot is open to every side, and hoppers and `get-item-handler`
    /// see it. Fails if there is no plugin block entity at the position.
    register-plugin-inventory: func(target-world: borrow<%world>, pos: block-pos, slot-count: u32, slot-limit: u8) -> result<_, string>;

    /// Takes the inventory away from the plugin block entity at a position and returns the items
    /// that were in it. Fails if there is no such entity, an entity without an inventory returns
    /// an empty list.
    unregister-plugin-inventory: func(target-world: borrow<%world>, pos: block-pos) -> result<list<item-stack>, string>;
}
